import json,csv
from pathlib import Path
import numpy as np
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent/'E15_threshold_calibration';r=json.loads((p/'run.json').read_text());z=np.load(p/'calibration_predictions.npz')
rows=[]
for item in r['calibrated_thresholds']:
 a=item['affordance'];t=float(item['threshold']);pos=r['calibration_objects'][a]['positive'];neg=r['calibration_objects'][a]['negative']
 pp=[z[f'{a}__{x["shape_id"]}__pred'] for x in pos];gts=[z[f'{a}__{x["shape_id"]}__gt'].astype(bool) for x in pos]
 nn=[z[f'{a}__{x["shape_id"]}__pred'] for x in neg]
 train_detect=int(sum(bool((x>=t).any()) for x in pp));train_rec=float(np.mean([((x>=t)&g).sum()/g.sum() for x,g in zip(pp,gts)]))
 ts=[x for x in r['test_summary'] if x['affordance']==a]
 def get(group,cond):return next(x for x in ts if x['group']==group and x['condition']==cond)
 pos0=get('positive','original');pos1=get('positive','selected_paraphrase');neg0=get('negative','original');neg1=get('negative','selected_paraphrase')
 max0=float(max(x['max_score'] for x in r['test_metrics'] if x['affordance']==a and x['group']=='positive' and x['condition']=='original'))
 max1=float(max(x['max_score'] for x in r['test_metrics'] if x['affordance']==a and x['group']=='positive' and x['condition']=='selected_paraphrase'))
 rows.append({'affordance':a,'threshold':t,'train_balanced_macro_iou':float(item['train_balanced_macro_iou']),'train_positive_objects_detected':train_detect,'train_positive_point_recall':train_rec,'train_negative_objects_flagged':int(sum(bool((x>=t).any()) for x in nn)),'test_max_original_score':max0,'test_max_paraphrase_score':max1,'test_positive_original_iou':float(pos0['iou_at_calibrated_threshold']),'test_positive_paraphrase_iou':float(pos1['iou_at_calibrated_threshold']),'test_positive_original_detected':int(round(20*pos0['object_alarm'])),'test_positive_paraphrase_detected':int(round(20*pos1['object_alarm'])),'test_negative_original_flagged':int(round(20*neg0['object_alarm'])),'test_negative_paraphrase_flagged':int(round(20*neg1['object_alarm']))})
r['threshold_diagnostics']=rows
(p/'run.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,allow_nan=True)+'\n')
with (p/'threshold_diagnostics.csv').open('w',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=rows[0].keys());w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
lines=['# E15: threshold calibration and validation transfer','','**Status:** complete on MPS. The goal was to set an action-specific cutoff from OpenAD training objects, then apply it unchanged to the positive/negative E14 validation objects for both original and selected paraphrase prompts. Train and validation shape IDs are disjoint. The prompts and model weights were fixed.','','## Result: the calibration objective collapsed to empty predictions','','For each affordance, the threshold maximized balanced mean object IoU on 40 positive and 40 negative training objects. On a negative object, predicting no points receives IoU 1.0. The optimizer therefore found the all-background solution for four of the five actions; on unlock it found almost the same result. This is a degenerate calibration result, not a useful deployment threshold.','', '| Affordance | Chosen threshold | Train positive objects detected at cutoff | Test positive original/paraphrase detected | Test negative original/paraphrase flagged |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in rows:lines.append(f"| {x['affordance']} | {x['threshold']:.2f} | {x['train_positive_objects_detected']}/40 | {x['test_positive_original_detected']}/20; {x['test_positive_paraphrase_detected']}/20 | {x['test_negative_original_flagged']}/20; {x['test_negative_paraphrase_flagged']}/20 |")
lines+=['','The selected cutoff exceeded the maximum original-query score on all E14 positive objects for every affordance. Consequently, the original query detected **0 of 20 positive objects for each action** at the calibrated cutoff. The selected paraphrase detected only one grab object, two wrap objects, and one accommodate object; it detected none for pour or unlock. Negative-object alarms were low because the cutoff suppressed nearly all predictions.','','## Interpretation','','The chosen threshold trades away nearly all target recall to suppress false alarms. That means the E14 increase in accommodate false alarms at 0.5 cannot be fixed simply by setting a high threshold without also losing target regions. The model scores do not cleanly separate the annotated positive and negative objects under this calibration objective. Threshold-free ranking metrics such as aIoU/AUC remain more informative for this study, while this cutoff result warns that point masks are difficult to obtain with a single threshold.','','This experiment exposed a metric-design problem: balanced macro IoU rewards empty predictions on negative objects, and on this sample that yields 0.50 even though positive recall is zero. The procedure and result are preserved; do not treat these cutoffs as recommended settings. E14 was analyzed earlier, so this is exploratory threshold transfer rather than an untouched final test.','','## Next experiment','','If thresholded masks matter to the proposal, set an operating rule in advance (for example, maximize positive recall while keeping negative-object alarms under a stated limit), calibrate it on training objects, and evaluate it on a separate, not-yet-inspected object split. Report the full precision-recall and false-alarm curve as well as the selected operating point. The current result should be described as a failed attempt to find a useful cutoff with balanced macro IoU.','','## Artifacts','','- `run.json`: prompts, sampled training objects, calibrated cutoffs, test metrics, and run metadata.\n- `calibration_predictions.npz`: training calibration maps and ground truth.\n- `threshold_diagnostics.csv`: cutoffs and detection counts.\n- `run.log`, `run_e15_threshold_calibration.py`, and `summarize_e15_threshold_calibration.py`: log and scripts.']
(p/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('\n'.join(lines[:20]))
